  "Question": "A circle is drawn with the origin \\(O\\) as its center and \\(r\\) as its radius. If point \\(A(3,4)\\) lies inside the circle, the range of \\(r\\) is",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(r>5\\)",
    "B": "\\(r<5\\)",
    "C": "\\(r>3\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(OA=\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5\\). For the point to lie inside the circle, \\(OA<r\\), so \\(r>5\\).",
